From 08d63f6d6b8f9282685e9cc70da89074191171cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:28:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10950/11362] ARC generalization-floor lint: word-boundary ARC
 scope; substring matched inside "research"
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The floor check's ARC-scope gate was a bare substring test ('"arc" in
prompt'). "research" contains "arc", and near-every task prompt in this
repo names research-roadmap / research_conductor / research-program. So
the scope gate passed for EVERY task, and one generic ML phrase such as
"held-out" completed a false match. The guard could not fail.

Concrete damage: milestone 2026.09.609 has 12 tasks and zero ARC work,
yet the lint printed "OK (soft): 3 generalization-testing-floor task(s)
detected". All 3 matches scoped in on the letters a-r-c inside
"research" and signalled on "held-out". This is the class-B failure the
QA-Layer discipline names: a pattern narrower (here: WIDER) than its
concept, in a guard that decides whether the floor is met.

Fix: _ARC_SCOPE word-boundary regex — the word "arc" (covers ARC,
ARC-AGI-3), arc_*/arc-*/arc3* identifiers (arc_solver_kit,
arc3_replay_scorecard), the live entrypoints E3AgentPolicy /
make_carnot_agent, the offline arcade, and arcprize — alongside the
existing _GAMES check. Kept generous toward ARC on purpose: a genuine
ARC task that stops counting would make the floor warn on compliant
roadmaps and teach readers to ignore it. Bonus caught by the new tests:
the OLD code also under-matched prompts naming only E3AgentPolicy or
make_carnot_agent (no a-r-c substring in either).

Spec: REQ-ARC-6861 + 3 SCENARIOs (openspec/capabilities/arc-agi/
spec.md). Tests: 4 new in tests/python/test_arc_levelup_guarantee_
lint.py, including the pinned 2026.09.609 roadmap fixture (counts 0;
the pre-fix predicate counted 3) and a words-containing-arc case
(research, archive, architecture, march, overarching). Mutation-
verified: hand-reverting the word boundary turns exactly those 4 tests
RED; restored byte-identical (cmp), 23/23 GREEN.

The corrected lint now reports the TRUE state of the live roadmap:
WARN (soft): 0 floor tasks on 2026.09.609. Stays WARN-only per the
CLAUDE.md "ARC-AGI-3 Generalization-Testing Floor" rule.

